- # `↯/s.112.5` — `Sse.Error`
+ # `↯/s.112.5` — `Sse.Error`

- Raised when Obligatory cannot parse a server-sent event.
+ Se lanza cuando Obligatory no puede analizar un evento enviado por el servidor.

- ## Cause
+ ## Causa

- SSE messages are framed as `field: value` lines, with `field`
- restricted to `event`, `data`, `id`, or `retry`. The `SseSource`
- class also enforces a replay-buffer capacity. When any of these
- expectations is violated, this error is raised. The constructor
- takes a `reason: Reason`; the rendered message is `the
+ Los mensajes SSE se entraman como líneas `field: value`, con `field` restringido a `event`, `data`,
+ `id` o `retry`. La clase `SseSource` impone además una capacidad del búfer de repetición. Cuando se
+ incumple cualquiera de estas expectativas, se lanza este error. El constructor toma un
+ `reason: Reason`; el mensaje que se muestra es `the

- server-sent event was not valid because $reason`.
+ server-sent event was not valid because $reason`.

- ## Variants
+ ## Variantes

- ### `↯/s.112.5.1` — `MalformedField`
+ ### `↯/s.112.5.1` — `MalformedField`

- A line in the SSE stream did not contain the required `:`
- separator between field name and value.
+ Una línea del flujo SSE no contenía el separador `:` obligatorio entre el nombre del campo y el
+ valor.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.112.5.1] the server-sent event was not valid because a line did not contain the expected field: value separator`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.112.5.1] the server-sent event was not valid because a line did not contain the expected field: value separator`

- **Resolution.** Verify the producer is emitting valid SSE frames;
- each non-empty line must contain a colon.
+ **Solución.** Comprueba que el productor emite tramas SSE válidas; cada línea no vacía debe contener
+ dos puntos.

- ### `↯/s.112.5.2` — `UnknownField`
+ ### `↯/s.112.5.2` — `UnknownField`

- A field name other than `event`, `data`, `id`, or `retry` was
- encountered.
+ Se encontró un nombre de campo distinto de `event`, `data`, `id` o `retry`.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.112.5.2] the server-sent event was not valid because the field name was not one of event, data, id, or retry`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.112.5.2] the server-sent event was not valid because the field name was not one of event, data, id, or retry`

- **Resolution.** Strip non-standard fields before parsing; or extend
- the parser to accept the field.
+ **Solución.** Elimina los campos no estándar antes del análisis, o amplía el analizador para que
+ acepte el campo.

- ### `↯/s.112.5.3` — `BadRetryValue`
+ ### `↯/s.112.5.3` — `BadRetryValue`

- The `retry` field's value was not a parseable integer.
+ El valor del campo `retry` no era un entero analizable.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.112.5.3] the server-sent event was not valid because the retry field value could not be parsed as an integer`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.112.5.3] the server-sent event was not valid because the retry field value could not be parsed as an integer`

- **Resolution.** The `retry` value must be a plain decimal integer
- (milliseconds).
+ **Solución.** El valor de `retry` debe ser un entero decimal sencillo (en milisegundos).

- ### `↯/s.112.5.4` — `CapacityExceeded`
+ ### `↯/s.112.5.4` — `CapacityExceeded`

- The replay range requested from `SseSource.stream(start)` was
- larger than the source's circular buffer capacity, so older events
- have been overwritten.
+ El rango de repetición pedido a `SseSource.stream(start)` era mayor que la capacidad del búfer
+ circular de la fuente, así que los eventos más antiguos se han sobrescrito.

- **Example.** `[↯/s.112.5.4] the server-sent event was not valid because the requested replay range exceeded the source buffer capacity`
+ **Ejemplo.** `[↯/s.112.5.4] the server-sent event was not valid because the requested replay range exceeded the source buffer capacity`

- **Resolution.** Increase the source's `capacity`, or request a more
- recent `start` index.
+ **Solución.** Aumenta la `capacity` de la fuente, o pide un índice `start` más reciente.

